'' =============================================================================
''
''   File....... test-so84-goertzel-last-term-lag.spin2
''   Purpose.... Decide prediction SO84 on SILICON
''   Authors.... Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''   E-mail..... stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started.... Sep 2026
''   Updated.... 25 Sep 2026
''
'' =============================================================================

{ WHAT IS TESTED (brief BRIEF-SO84, Parts 2 and 5)
    Prediction: in DDS/Goertzel mode the per-clock term register (acca) and the
    readable accumulator (accx) update on the same clock edge, so accx adds the
    term acca held BEFORE the edge. A burst of N active clocks therefore adds
    L + T[1] + ... + T[N-1] to accx (L = the term acca held when the burst
    began) and leaves T[N] stranded in acca, which no instruction reads. The
    last term is not lost: the NEXT Goertzel burst adds it on its first clock.
    Nobody has observed this on a part; this program is written to be able to
    show it WRONG.

  RIG
    P2 Edge (or any P2), no jumper, nothing attached to P3. Pins P0..P7 free.
    The measuring cog drives P3 itself as a plain output (WRPIN 0, DIR=1, OUT
    fixed), so the Goertzel input bit 4g+3 (g = 0 -> P3) holds a steady level.
    Silicon Doc: in non-smart-pin modes the 'A' input drives IN, and 'A'
    defaults to "this pin's read state" -- the pad level, which is the driven
    level. The program does not assume this: it reads IN (TESTP) before and
    after every sequence and gates on it, and the sign of C must flip when the
    level flips (below), which proves the streamer sees the bit.
    If P3 is wired to anything on your board, remove it -- the cog drives P3.
    No DAC output is enabled on any pin (mode bits [11:8] = 0).

  DEBUGGER (EF-057)
    DEBUG_COGS = %0000_0001: the debug interrupt lives in cog 0 only. ALL
    streamer work and every GETXACC runs in a dedicated PASM cog started by
    COGINIT from the DAT block below; cog 0 only reads the hub mailbox and
    reports. (EF-057: with the default mask the debug ISR in the streaming cog
    corrupted Goertzel accumulators by millions.)

  CONSTRUCTION (brief Part 2, "Constructing a burst...")
    Mode word D = $F007_0000 + count: [15:12]=%1111 and [2:0]=%111 (Goertzel),
      [11:8]=0 (no DACs), [7]=0 (sinc1 -> acca REPLACED each clock), [6:3]=0
      (pin group 0 = P0..P3).
    IMM (S): K burst = $0000_80C3: imm[15]=1 (sum pin 4g+3 only), imm[14:12]=0,
      imm[19]=0, imm[11:9]=0, imm[8:0]=$0C3 (LUT address).
             Z burst = $0000_00C3: identical with imm[15:12]=0 -> every term 0.
             Z bursts always use count 4.
    LUT: every one of the 512 longs is written with $2513_0000 once, before the
      first burst (cos byte [23:16] = $13 = 19, sin byte [31:24] = $25 = 37).
      Filling ALL addresses (not just $0C3) makes the term independent of the
      LUT address and of the brief's INFERRED stale first LUT read.
      LUT sharing explicitly OFF (SETLUTS #0 = reset state). Read back at 3
      addresses and gated.
    Frequency: SETXFRQ $8000_0000 once at cog start (= the reset value the
      brief requires) so nco[31] is set every clock and a count-N burst is N
      enabled edges. No SETQ precedes any XINIT (no "queued" frequency).
    Term C: imm[19]=0, so the term is +g when the pin bit is 1 and -g when 0.
      Predicted Cx = -19 (P3 LOW), +19 (P3 HIGH). Cy = -37 / +37.

  HOW C IS ESTABLISHED (C is not directly readable)
    C_meas = (R2-B)[N=65] - (R2-B)[N=64], same level, same repetition. Under
    EVERY hypothesis named below (lag, no lag, lost term) this difference is
    exactly one term, so it measures C without assuming the answer. Gate:
    |C_meas| = 19, the same in every repetition of a level, and opposite in
    sign between P3 LOW and P3 HIGH. Every delta must be a whole multiple of
    19. The measured C (with its sign) is then the unit for classification;
    whether its sign matches the brief's rule is reported separately.

  ONE SEQUENCE (brief Part 5, run for N = 64 and N = 65, each from its own
  start; every read is taken with the streamer idle: WAIT_IDLE = 500 clocks
  after each XINIT, > N + 16)
    B0  : read, before anything        (follows a Z burst from the prior step)
    Z   : zero burst, wait; read B      [start: sets held term L = 0]
    K   : count-N burst, wait; read R1; wait 1000 clocks more; read R1b
    Z   : zero burst, wait; read R2     [the idiom: flushes the held term]
    --- carry arm (my addition, after the brief's sequence is complete) ---
    K   : count-N burst, wait; read R3
    K   : count-N burst, wait; read R4  [second K right after the first]
    Z   : zero burst, wait; read R5
    d1 = R1-B, d2 = R2-R1, d3 = R3-R2, d4 = R4-R3, d5 = R5-R4.

  ARMS / RUN ORDER
    prime Z burst; then P3 LOW: 4 repetitions x (N=64, N=65); then P3 HIGH:
    4 repetitions x (N=64, N=65) = 16 recorded sequences.

  IN-RUN CONTROLS (gating -- a failure prints RIG FAIL and NO verdict)
    LUT   : readback of LUT[$0C3], LUT[0], LUT[$1FF] = $2513_0000.
    PIN   : TESTP P3 before and after every sequence = the driven level.
    ZZ    : B - B0 = 0 (a zero burst after a zero burst adds nothing; true
            under every named hypothesis).
    MULT  : d1..d5 whole multiples of 19.
    C     : |C_meas| = 19, constant per level, sign flips with P3.
  PREMISE CHECKS (the brief names these as NOT-PROVEN outcomes)
    IDLE  : R1b - R1 = 0 in every sequence. Nonzero -> REFUTED (accx moved
            while idle) -- unless it moved by >= 500*19, which means the burst
            never ended (construction failed) -> INCONCLUSIVE.
    RUN-ON: if the ZZ control fails ONLY because B reads 0 after a nonzero B0,
            accx is being cleared by a read -> REFUTED (reads are not the
            running totals the brief traces).

  PREDICTIONS, accx, in units of the measured C (written before the run)
    TRUE  (lag, brief)  : R1b-R1 = 0, d1 = (N-1)*C, d2 = C  (R2-B = N*C)
                          carry arm: d3 = (N-1)*C, d4 = N*C, d5 = C
    FALSE (no lag)      : d1 = N*C,     d2 = 0   (carry: N*C, N*C, 0)
    FALSE (lost term)   : d1 = (N-1)*C, d2 = 0   (carry: (N-1)C, (N-1)C, 0)
    FALSE (idle move)   : R1b - R1 <> 0
    Numbers, N=64: TRUE d1 = 63C, d2 = C; no-lag 64C, 0; lost 63C, 0.
             N=65: TRUE d1 = 64C, d2 = C; no-lag 65C, 0; lost 64C, 0.
    With C = +19: N=64 TRUE d1 = 1197, d2 = 19 | no-lag 1216, 0 | lost 1197, 0
                  N=65 TRUE d1 = 1216, d2 = 19 | no-lag 1235, 0 | lost 1216, 0
    (C = -19 negates every number.) The program prints this table too.

  VERDICT RULE (one line, "VERDICT: ...")
    CONFIRMED    : all 16 sequences read the TRUE pair AND the carry arm.
    REFUTED      : every sequence of a given N reads the same non-TRUE pair
                   (named: no lag / lost term; else printed as d1=(N+a)*C,
                   d2=b*C); or the premise checks above fail.
    INCONCLUSIVE : results not repeatable across repetitions/levels; or Part 5
                   pair TRUE but the carry arm disagrees; or burst never ended.
    accy (sin byte, |C| = 37) is reported as CORROBORATION only; the brief
    traces accx, and the sin byte's position is from the KB, not the brief.

  DEPENDS ON CLAIMS THE BRIEF MARKS INFERRED / UNDETERMINED
    - "same clock does not mean same value" (nonblocking semantics): INFERRED;
      it IS the claim under test -- the discriminator decides it.
    - zero-burst idiom (Part 4/5): INFERRED; d2 decides it.
    - LUT read one clock late: INFERRED; neutralised by filling all 512 longs
      identically and priming with a Z burst before the first K burst.
    - pin input path: UNDETERMINED; guarded by the PIN control and by the
      sign-flip requirement on C_meas.
    - GETXACC result latency: UNDETERMINED; irrelevant here (reads idle only,
      standard GETXACC + "mov y, 0-0" follower).

  VERIFIED OPCODES (pnut-ts v1.55.8, `pnut-ts -d -l`, read from the .lst hex
  dump; hub offsets are object-relative, cog addresses in brackets):
    getxacc b0x_ [$070]      $FD60E01E  [27:21]=1101011, [8:0]=000011110 (= brief's
                                         op2 pattern; D=$070). All 8 GETXACCs
                                         share the form $FD60xx1E.
    mov b0y_, 0-0            $F600E200  S=0: the follower that receives accy
    xinit dz_, imz_          $FCA0C061  [27:19]=110010100 (brief: 1100101_0?),
                                         L=I=0, D=$060 (dz_), S=$061 (imz_)
    xinit dk_, imk_          $FCA0D662  same pattern, D=$06B (dk_), S=$062 (imk_)
    setxfrq freq80_          $FD60B41D  [8:0]=000011101, L=0, D=$05A (freq80_)
    wrlut lutv_, ii_         $FC30B663  [27:21]=1100001, [20]=1, L=I=0,
                                         D=$05B (lutv_), S=$063 (ii_ = 511..0)
    setluts #0               $FD640037  [8:0]=000110111, L=1, D=0 (sharing off)
    wrpin #0, #3             $FC0C0003  smart pin off, reset config on P3
    drvl #3 / drvh #3        $FD640658 / $FD640659 (if_z / if_nz forms $A.., $5..)
    testp #3 wc              $FD740640
    waitx ##500 / ##1000     AUGD $FF800000 + $FD67E81F / AUGD $FF800001 + $FD67D01F
    setq #19 + wrlong rlevel_,ptrb   $FD642628 + $FC64D980 (20-long record)
    DAT longs as assembled:
      dmode_  = $F007_0000 : [31:28]=%1111 (mode [15:12]), [27:24]=%0000 (DAC
                field [11:8]), [23]=0 (sinc1, mode [7]), [22:19]=%0000 (pin
                group, mode [6:3]), [18:16]=%111 (mode [2:0])  -- Goertzel row
      dz_     = $F007_0004 (zero burst, count 4)
      imz_    = $0000_00C3 (imm[15:12]=0, imm[8:0]=$0C3)
      imk_    = $0000_80C3 (imm[15]=1, imm[14:12]=0, imm[19:16]=0, [11:9]=0)
      lutv_   = $2513_0000   freq80_ = $8000_0000
    dk_ is built at run time as dmode_ OR N -> $F007_0040 / $F007_0041.

  HOW TO RUN
    Compile: pnut-ts -d test-so84-goertzel-last-term-lag.spin2
    Load with pnut-term-ts (or PNut) with DEBUG enabled, 2 Mbaud default.
    The engine finishes in well under 1 ms; the report prints ~125 lines.
    Success looks like: no RIG FAIL lines, "C measured" line shows -19 / +19,
    and a single "VERDICT: ..." line near the end, then "=== END ===".
}

CON ' ---- Rig Parameters ----
  _clkfreq   = 200_000_000
  DEBUG_COGS = %0000_0001                ' EF-057: debugger in cog 0 ONLY

  PIN        = 3                         ' Goertzel input 4g+3, pin group g = 0
  G_COS      = $13                       ' LUT bits [23:16] -> |Cx| = 19
  G_SIN      = $25                       ' LUT bits [31:24] -> |Cy| = 37 (corroborating)
  LUT_ADDR   = $0C3
  LUTV       = (G_SIN << 24) | (G_COS << 16)     ' $2513_0000
  MODE_G     = $F007_0000                ' Goertzel sinc1, DACs off, pin group 0
  IMM_K      = $0000_8000 | LUT_ADDR     ' imm[15]=1, imm[19]=0, imm[11:9]=0
  IMM_Z      = LUT_ADDR                  ' imm[15:12]=0 -> every term zero
  ZCOUNT     = 4
  N_A        = 64
  N_B        = 65
  REPS       = 4
  WAIT_IDLE  = 500                       ' > N + 16 clocks after XINIT
  WAIT_R1B   = 1000                      ' the brief's "further 1000 clocks"
  WAIT_PIN   = 10_000                    ' settle after changing P3
  HDR        = 4                         ' mailbox header longs
  RECL       = 20                        ' longs per recorded sequence
  NREC       = 2 * REPS * 2              ' levels x reps x lengths = 16
  MBOX_DONE  = 1                         ' mbox[0] sentinel: engine cog finished
  RIG_TIMEOUT_SEC = 2                    ' host wait cap; engine finishes in << 1 ms
  DELTA_COUNT = 5                        ' d1..d5 checked by check_multiples()

  ' record layout -- MUST match the RES order rlevel_..r5y_ in the DAT
  #0, O_LEVEL, O_N, O_PINB, O_PINA, O_B0X, O_B0Y, O_BX, O_BY, O_R1X, O_R1Y, O_R1BX, O_R1BY, O_R2X, O_R2Y, O_R3X, O_R3Y, O_R4X, O_R4Y, O_R5X, O_R5Y

  ' channel selectors for the analysis
  CH_X       = 0
  CH_Y       = 1

  ' P3 drive levels for the arm loop (predicted C sign flips between these)
  LEVEL_LOW  = 0
  LEVEL_HIGH = 1

VAR ' ---- Mailbox & Scoring State ----
  long mbox[HDR + NREC * RECL]           ' [0] done [1..3] LUT readbacks, then records
  long cm[2 * 2 * REPS]                  ' measured C: [ch*8 + level*4 + rep]
  long cmeas[2 * 2]                      ' accepted C: [ch*2 + level]
  long ka[NREC], kb[NREC]                ' main pair: d1/C - N, d2/C
  long k3[NREC], k4[NREC], k5[NREC]      ' carry arm: d3/C - N, d4/C - N, d5/C
  long nfail


PUB main() | engineCog, tstart
'' Run the SO84 rig: start the measuring engine cog, wait for its mailbox
'' done-flag, then print the full report and verdict.

  longfill(@mbox, 0, HDR + NREC * RECL)
  debug("=== SO84: does accx trail acca by one active clock? ===")
  predictions()
  engineCog := coginit(COGEXEC_NEW, @engine, @mbox)
  if engineCog < 0
    debug("RIG FAIL: no free cog for the measuring engine")
    finish()
  tstart := getct()
  repeat until mbox[0] == MBOX_DONE or (getct() - tstart) > clkfreq * RIG_TIMEOUT_SEC
  if mbox[0] <> MBOX_DONE
    cogstop(engineCog)
    debug("RIG FAIL: measuring cog did not report done within 2 s (expected < 1 ms)")
    finish()
  debug("measuring cog = ", udec_(engineCog), " (debugger restricted to cog 0)")
  report()
  finish()


PRI finish()
' Every terminal path ends here. pnut-term-ts ends the run when END_SESSION or
' DEBUG_END_SESSION appears in the output (--headless or --exit-on-end-session).

  debug("=== END ===")
  debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")
  repeat


PRI cpred(ch, lvl) : termC
' Predicted per-clock term C for a channel at a given P3 level.
'
' @param ch - channel selector (CH_X or CH_Y)
' @param lvl - P3 level (LEVEL_LOW or LEVEL_HIGH)
' @returns termC - predicted signed term magnitude/sign for this channel+level

  if ch == CH_X
    termC := G_COS
  else
    termC := G_SIN
  if lvl == LEVEL_LOW
    termC := -termC


PRI predictions() | lvl, burstN, predC
' Print the fixed-before-the-run prediction table for every (P3 level, N)
' combination, under each named hypothesis.

  debug("PREDICTIONS for accx, fixed before the run (C = per-clock term):")
  debug("  brief sign rule, imm[19]=0: C = -19 with P3 LOW, +19 with P3 HIGH")
  debug("  TRUE  (lag, brief): R1b-R1 = 0, d1 = (N-1)*C, d2 = C (R2-B = N*C)")
  debug("  FALSE (no lag)    : d1 = N*C, d2 = 0")
  debug("  FALSE (lost term) : d1 = (N-1)*C, d2 = 0")
  debug("  FALSE (idle move) : R1b-R1 <> 0")
  debug("  carry arm TRUE d3=(N-1)C d4=N*C d5=C | no-lag N*C,N*C,0 | lost (N-1)C,(N-1)C,0")
  repeat lvl from LEVEL_LOW to LEVEL_HIGH
    predC := cpred(CH_X, lvl)
    repeat burstN from N_A to N_B
      debug("  P3=", udec_(lvl), " N=", udec_(burstN), " C=", sdec_(predC), ": TRUE d1=", sdec_((burstN - 1) * predC), " d2=", sdec_(predC), " | no-lag d1=", sdec_(burstN * predC), " d2=0 | lost d1=", sdec_((burstN - 1) * predC), " d2=0")


PRI rv(seqIdx, fieldOff) : fieldVal
' Read one field from one recorded sequence in the mailbox.
'
' @param seqIdx - sequence index, 0..NREC-1
' @param fieldOff - record field offset (an O_xxx constant)
' @returns fieldVal - the recorded value

  fieldVal := mbox[HDR + seqIdx * RECL + fieldOff]


PRI dd(seqIdx, offLater, offEarlier) : deltaVal
' Delta between two fields of the same recorded sequence (later - earlier).
'
' @param seqIdx - sequence index, 0..NREC-1
' @param offLater - record field offset of the later reading
' @param offEarlier - record field offset of the earlier reading
' @returns deltaVal - offLater's value minus offEarlier's value

  deltaVal := rv(seqIdx, offLater) - rv(seqIdx, offEarlier)


PRI report() | seqIdx, bContinue
' Print every raw record, run the gating controls and premise checks in
' order, and print the verdict if every gate upstream of it passed. Single
' exit: bContinue gates each stage instead of returning early.

  nfail := 0
  check_lut()
  debug(" ")
  debug("--- RAW DATA (signed decimal; every sequence) ---")
  repeat seqIdx from 0 to NREC - 1
    print_record(seqIdx)
  debug(" ")
  debug("--- CONTROLS ---")
  check_pins()
  bContinue := (nfail == 0)
  if not bContinue
    debug("NO VERDICT: a rig control failed (see RIG FAIL lines above)")
  if bContinue
    bContinue := idle_premise()
  if bContinue
    bContinue := runon_premise()
  if bContinue
    check_multiples(CH_X)
    measure_c(CH_X)
    bContinue := (nfail == 0)
    if not bContinue
      debug("NO VERDICT: a construction control failed (see RIG FAIL lines above)")
  if bContinue
    debug("controls: LUT ok, pin ok, idle ok (R1b-R1 = 0), zero-after-zero ok, all deltas whole multiples of 19, C ok")
    debug(" ")
    accy_summary()
    debug(" ")
    classify_and_verdict()


PRI check_lut()
' Verify the LUT readback (all three sampled addresses) matches what the
' engine wrote; a mismatch is a rig construction failure, not a data point.

  debug("LUT readback [$0C3]=", uhex_long_(mbox[1]), " [0]=", uhex_long_(mbox[2]), " [$1FF]=", uhex_long_(mbox[3]), "  expected ", uhex_long_(LUTV))
  if mbox[1] <> LUTV or mbox[2] <> LUTV or mbox[3] <> LUTV
    debug("RIG FAIL: LUT readback, expected ", uhex_long_(LUTV), " at all three addresses")
    nfail++


PRI print_record(seqIdx)
' Print the raw B0/B/R1/R1b/R2/R3/R4/R5 readings and every delta for one
' recorded sequence, on both channels.
'
' @param seqIdx - sequence index, 0..NREC-1

  debug("#", udec_(seqIdx), " P3=", udec_(rv(seqIdx, O_LEVEL)), " rep=", udec_((seqIdx / 2) // REPS), " N=", udec_(rv(seqIdx, O_N)), " pin IN before/after=", udec_(rv(seqIdx, O_PINB)), "/", udec_(rv(seqIdx, O_PINA)))
  debug("   accx B0=", sdec_long_(rv(seqIdx, O_B0X)), " B=", sdec_long_(rv(seqIdx, O_BX)), " R1=", sdec_long_(rv(seqIdx, O_R1X)), " R1b=", sdec_long_(rv(seqIdx, O_R1BX)), " R2=", sdec_long_(rv(seqIdx, O_R2X)), " R3=", sdec_long_(rv(seqIdx, O_R3X)), " R4=", sdec_long_(rv(seqIdx, O_R4X)), " R5=", sdec_long_(rv(seqIdx, O_R5X)))
  debug("   accy B0=", sdec_long_(rv(seqIdx, O_B0Y)), " B=", sdec_long_(rv(seqIdx, O_BY)), " R1=", sdec_long_(rv(seqIdx, O_R1Y)), " R1b=", sdec_long_(rv(seqIdx, O_R1BY)), " R2=", sdec_long_(rv(seqIdx, O_R2Y)), " R3=", sdec_long_(rv(seqIdx, O_R3Y)), " R4=", sdec_long_(rv(seqIdx, O_R4Y)), " R5=", sdec_long_(rv(seqIdx, O_R5Y)))
  debug("   dx: B-B0=", sdec_(dd(seqIdx, O_BX, O_B0X)), " d1=", sdec_(dd(seqIdx, O_R1X, O_BX)), " R1b-R1=", sdec_(dd(seqIdx, O_R1BX, O_R1X)), " d2=", sdec_(dd(seqIdx, O_R2X, O_R1X)), " d3=", sdec_(dd(seqIdx, O_R3X, O_R2X)), " d4=", sdec_(dd(seqIdx, O_R4X, O_R3X)), " d5=", sdec_(dd(seqIdx, O_R5X, O_R4X)))
  debug("   dy: B-B0=", sdec_(dd(seqIdx, O_BY, O_B0Y)), " d1=", sdec_(dd(seqIdx, O_R1Y, O_BY)), " R1b-R1=", sdec_(dd(seqIdx, O_R1BY, O_R1Y)), " d2=", sdec_(dd(seqIdx, O_R2Y, O_R1Y)), " d3=", sdec_(dd(seqIdx, O_R3Y, O_R2Y)), " d4=", sdec_(dd(seqIdx, O_R4Y, O_R3Y)), " d5=", sdec_(dd(seqIdx, O_R5Y, O_R4Y)))


PRI check_pins() | seqIdx, lvl
' Verify TESTP read the driven level, before and after, on every sequence.

  repeat seqIdx from 0 to NREC - 1
    lvl := rv(seqIdx, O_LEVEL)
    if rv(seqIdx, O_PINB) <> lvl or rv(seqIdx, O_PINA) <> lvl
      debug("RIG FAIL: pin control, seq #", udec_(seqIdx), " expected P3 IN = ", udec_(lvl), " got before/after ", udec_(rv(seqIdx, O_PINB)), "/", udec_(rv(seqIdx, O_PINA)))
      nfail++


PRI idle_premise() : bIdleOk | seqIdx, deltaVal, nbad, worst
' The brief's premise: accx does not move while the streamer is idle.
'
' @returns bIdleOk - TRUE when R1b = R1 in every sequence; FALSE prints the
'   verdict (INCONCLUSIVE or REFUTED) before returning

  nbad := 0
  worst := 0
  repeat seqIdx from 0 to NREC - 1
    deltaVal := dd(seqIdx, O_R1BX, O_R1X)
    if deltaVal
      nbad++
      if abs deltaVal > worst
        worst := abs deltaVal
  bIdleOk := (nbad == 0)
  if not bIdleOk
    debug("PREMISE FAIL: R1b-R1 nonzero in ", udec_(nbad), " of 16 sequences, largest |R1b-R1| = ", udec_(worst))
    if worst >= (WAIT_R1B / 2) * G_COS
      debug("VERDICT: INCONCLUSIVE - accx still moving ~1000 clocks after the burst: the count-down (burst end) of the construction did not hold")
    else
      debug("VERDICT: REFUTED - accx moved while the streamer was idle (R1b-R1 <> 0); the premise every reading rests on fails")


PRI runon_premise() : bRunonOk | seqIdx, nbad, nclr, nb0
' ZZ control: a zero burst after a zero burst adds nothing (every hypothesis).
' If it fails ONLY because B reads 0 after a nonzero B0, accx is being cleared
' by a read (not running totals) -- the brief's traced idle-read claim fails.
'
' @returns bRunonOk - TRUE when the ZZ control holds in every sequence; FALSE
'   prints the verdict before returning

  nbad := 0
  nclr := 0
  nb0 := 0
  repeat seqIdx from 0 to NREC - 1
    if rv(seqIdx, O_B0X)
      nb0++
    if dd(seqIdx, O_BX, O_B0X)
      nbad++
      if rv(seqIdx, O_BX) == 0
        nclr++
  bRunonOk := (nbad == 0)
  if not bRunonOk
    if nclr == nbad and nclr == nb0
      debug("PREMISE FAIL: in every sequence with B0 <> 0 (", udec_(nb0), ") a zero burst then read B = 0")
      debug("  Under clear-on-read semantics read d1 = R1 and d2 = R2 directly from the raw rows above.")
      debug("VERDICT: REFUTED - accx does not run on across reads: a GETXACC clears it (at the read or at the next burst)")
    else
      debug("RIG FAIL: zero-burst control, B-B0 <> 0 in ", udec_(nbad), " of 16 sequences (expected 0: a zero burst after a zero burst adds nothing)")
      debug("NO VERDICT: the zero burst does not behave as constructed")


PRI check_multiples(ch) : nbad | seqIdx, magC, chOff, deltaIdx, deltaVal
' Verify d1..d5 are whole multiples of the channel's term magnitude, in
' every sequence. Only channel CH_X's failures fold into nfail (gating);
' CH_Y (accy) is corroborating only.
'
' @param ch - channel selector (CH_X or CH_Y)
' @returns nbad - count of non-multiple deltas found for this channel

  if ch == CH_X
    magC := G_COS
    chOff := 0
  else
    magC := G_SIN
    chOff := 1
  nbad := 0
  repeat seqIdx from 0 to NREC - 1
    repeat deltaIdx from 0 to DELTA_COUNT - 1
      case deltaIdx
        0: deltaVal := dd(seqIdx, O_R1X + chOff, O_BX + chOff)
        1: deltaVal := dd(seqIdx, O_R2X + chOff, O_R1X + chOff)
        2: deltaVal := dd(seqIdx, O_R3X + chOff, O_R2X + chOff)
        3: deltaVal := dd(seqIdx, O_R4X + chOff, O_R3X + chOff)
        4: deltaVal := dd(seqIdx, O_R5X + chOff, O_R4X + chOff)
      if deltaVal // magC
        nbad++
        if ch == CH_X
          debug("RIG FAIL: multiple-of-C control, seq #", udec_(seqIdx), " d", udec_(deltaIdx + 1), " = ", sdec_(deltaVal), " is not a whole multiple of ", udec_(magC))
  if ch == CH_X
    nfail += nbad


PRI measure_c(ch) : bad | lvl, rp, seqIdx, chOff, magC, measC, measC0
' C_meas = (R2-B)[N=65] - (R2-B)[N=64], same level and repetition: one term
' under every named hypothesis. Gate (accx only): |C| = 19, constant per level,
' sign flips with P3.
'
' @param ch - channel selector (CH_X or CH_Y)
' @returns bad - count of C-control failures found for this channel

  if ch == CH_X
    magC := G_COS
    chOff := 0
  else
    magC := G_SIN
    chOff := 1
  bad := 0
  repeat lvl from LEVEL_LOW to LEVEL_HIGH
    repeat rp from 0 to REPS - 1
      seqIdx := (lvl * REPS + rp) * 2
      measC := dd(seqIdx + 1, O_R2X + chOff, O_BX + chOff) - dd(seqIdx, O_R2X + chOff, O_BX + chOff)
      cm[ch * 8 + lvl * 4 + rp] := measC
      if rp == 0
        measC0 := measC
      if abs measC <> magC or measC <> measC0
        bad++
        if ch == CH_X
          debug("RIG FAIL: C control, P3=", udec_(lvl), " rep ", udec_(rp), " C_meas = ", sdec_(measC), " (expected |C| = ", udec_(magC), ", same in every rep)")
    cmeas[ch * 2 + lvl] := measC0
  if cmeas[ch * 2 + 0] <> -cmeas[ch * 2 + 1]
    bad++
    if ch == CH_X
      debug("RIG FAIL: C control, sign did not flip with P3: C(LOW) = ", sdec_(cmeas[0]), " C(HIGH) = ", sdec_(cmeas[1]))
  if ch == CH_X
    debug("C measured, accx: P3 LOW reps ", sdec_(cm[0]), " ", sdec_(cm[1]), " ", sdec_(cm[2]), " ", sdec_(cm[3]), " | P3 HIGH reps ", sdec_(cm[4]), " ", sdec_(cm[5]), " ", sdec_(cm[6]), " ", sdec_(cm[7]), "  (predicted -19 / +19)")
    if bad == 0
      if cmeas[0] == -G_COS
        debug("  sign rule: as the brief states (term = +g when imm[19] differs from the pin bit)")
      else
        debug("  sign rule: INVERTED relative to the brief (not gating; classification uses the measured C)")
    nfail += bad


PRI class_name(d1Code, d2Code) : pLabel
' Human-readable label for a Part-5 pair classification.
'
' @param d1Code - d1/C - N (should be -1 under TRUE, 0 under no-lag/lost)
' @param d2Code - d2/C (should be 1 under TRUE, 0 under no-lag/lost)
' @returns pLabel - address of the matching label string

  if d1Code == -1 and d2Code == 1
    pLabel := string("TRUE (lag): d1=(N-1)C d2=C")
  elseif d1Code == 0 and d2Code == 0
    pLabel := string("FALSE (no lag): d1=N*C d2=0")
  elseif d1Code == -1 and d2Code == 0
    pLabel := string("FALSE (lost term): d1=(N-1)C d2=0")
  else
    pLabel := string("OTHER")


PRI carry_name(d3Code, d4Code, d5Code) : pLabel
' Human-readable label for the carry-arm classification.
'
' @param d3Code - d3/C - N
' @param d4Code - d4/C - N
' @param d5Code - d5/C
' @returns pLabel - address of the matching label string

  if d3Code == -1 and d4Code == 0 and d5Code == 1
    pLabel := string("TRUE (lag)")
  elseif d3Code == 0 and d4Code == 0 and d5Code == 0
    pLabel := string("no-lag")
  elseif d3Code == -1 and d4Code == -1 and d5Code == 0
    pLabel := string("lost")
  else
    pLabel := string("OTHER")


PRI classify_and_verdict() | seqIdx, burstN, measC, same64, same65, idx64, idx65, allcarry, ntrue, nnolag, nlost, nother
' Classify every sequence's Part-5 pair and carry arm against the named
' hypotheses, then print the final VERDICT line.

  debug("--- CLASSIFICATION (accx, units of measured C) ---")
  allcarry := TRUE
  ntrue := 0
  nnolag := 0
  nlost := 0
  nother := 0
  repeat seqIdx from 0 to NREC - 1
    burstN := rv(seqIdx, O_N)
    measC := cmeas[rv(seqIdx, O_LEVEL)]
    ka[seqIdx] := dd(seqIdx, O_R1X, O_BX) / measC - burstN
    kb[seqIdx] := dd(seqIdx, O_R2X, O_R1X) / measC
    k3[seqIdx] := dd(seqIdx, O_R3X, O_R2X) / measC - burstN
    k4[seqIdx] := dd(seqIdx, O_R4X, O_R3X) / measC - burstN
    k5[seqIdx] := dd(seqIdx, O_R5X, O_R4X) / measC
    debug("#", udec_(seqIdx), " N=", udec_(burstN), " C=", sdec_(measC), "  d1=(N", sdec_(ka[seqIdx]), ")C d2=", sdec_(kb[seqIdx]), "C -> ", zstr_(class_name(ka[seqIdx], kb[seqIdx])), " | carry d3=(N", sdec_(k3[seqIdx]), ")C d4=(N", sdec_(k4[seqIdx]), ")C d5=", sdec_(k5[seqIdx]), "C -> ", zstr_(carry_name(k3[seqIdx], k4[seqIdx], k5[seqIdx])))
    if not (k3[seqIdx] == -1 and k4[seqIdx] == 0 and k5[seqIdx] == 1)
      allcarry := FALSE
    if ka[seqIdx] == -1 and kb[seqIdx] == 1
      ntrue++
    elseif ka[seqIdx] == 0 and kb[seqIdx] == 0
      nnolag++
    elseif ka[seqIdx] == -1 and kb[seqIdx] == 0
      nlost++
    else
      nother++

  ' records alternate N=64 (even index) and N=65 (odd index)
  same64 := TRUE
  same65 := TRUE
  repeat seqIdx from 2 to NREC - 1
    if seqIdx & 1
      if ka[seqIdx] <> ka[1] or kb[seqIdx] <> kb[1]
        same65 := FALSE
    else
      if ka[seqIdx] <> ka[0] or kb[seqIdx] <> kb[0]
        same64 := FALSE
  idx64 := 0
  idx65 := 1
  debug("counts over 16 sequences: TRUE ", udec_(ntrue), "  no-lag ", udec_(nnolag), "  lost ", udec_(nlost), "  other ", udec_(nother))
  debug(" ")
  if ntrue == NREC
    if allcarry
      debug("VERDICT: CONFIRMED - all 16 sequences (N=64,65; P3 low,high; 4 reps) read d1=(N-1)C, d2=C, R1b-R1=0, and the carry arm read (N-1)C, N*C, C")
    else
      debug("VERDICT: INCONCLUSIVE - Part 5 pair is TRUE in all 16 sequences but the carry arm (two K bursts back to back) did not read (N-1)C, N*C, C in every one")
  elseif same64 and same65
    if ka[idx64] == ka[idx65] and kb[idx64] == kb[idx65]
      if ka[idx64] == 0 and kb[idx64] == 0
        debug("VERDICT: REFUTED - no lag: d1 = N*C and d2 = 0 at both lengths, every sequence")
      elseif ka[idx64] == -1 and kb[idx64] == 0
        debug("VERDICT: REFUTED - last term LOST, not late: d1 = (N-1)*C and d2 = 0 at both lengths, every sequence")
      else
        debug("VERDICT: REFUTED - neither lag, no-lag nor lost: every sequence reads d1 = (N", sdec_(ka[idx64]), ")*C, d2 = ", sdec_(kb[idx64]), "*C")
    else
      debug("VERDICT: REFUTED - length-dependent: N=64 reads d1=(N", sdec_(ka[idx64]), ")C d2=", sdec_(kb[idx64]), "C; N=65 reads d1=(N", sdec_(ka[idx65]), ")C d2=", sdec_(kb[idx65]), "C (repeatable per length)")
  else
    debug("VERDICT: INCONCLUSIVE - not repeatable across repetitions/levels: TRUE ", udec_(ntrue), " no-lag ", udec_(nnolag), " lost ", udec_(nlost), " other ", udec_(nother), " of 16")


PRI accy_summary() | seqIdx, burstN, measC, nidle, nzz, nmul, bad, nTrue, nCarry
' accy: corroborating only. The brief says accb/accy behave "identically";
' the sin byte's LUT position ([31:24]) comes from the KB, not the brief.
'
' Single exit: the TRUE/carry classification loop runs only when the accy
' construction checks passed; either way the method falls through to the end.

  debug("--- ACCY (corroborating only, not gating; predicted |C| = 37) ---")
  nidle := 0
  nzz := 0
  repeat seqIdx from 0 to NREC - 1
    if dd(seqIdx, O_R1BY, O_R1Y)
      nidle++
    if dd(seqIdx, O_BY, O_B0Y)
      nzz++
  nmul := check_multiples(CH_Y)
  bad := measure_c(CH_Y)
  debug("accy: idle moves ", udec_(nidle), ", zero-after-zero moves ", udec_(nzz), ", non-multiples of 37: ", udec_(nmul), ", C_meas P3 LOW ", sdec_(cm[8]), " ", sdec_(cm[9]), " ", sdec_(cm[10]), " ", sdec_(cm[11]), " HIGH ", sdec_(cm[12]), " ", sdec_(cm[13]), " ", sdec_(cm[14]), " ", sdec_(cm[15]))
  if nidle or nzz or nmul or bad
    debug("ACCY: construction checks failed on accy; no accy classification (accx verdict unaffected)")
  else
    nTrue := 0
    nCarry := 0
    repeat seqIdx from 0 to NREC - 1
      burstN := rv(seqIdx, O_N)
      measC := cmeas[2 + rv(seqIdx, O_LEVEL)]
      if dd(seqIdx, O_R1Y, O_BY) / measC - burstN == -1 and dd(seqIdx, O_R2Y, O_R1Y) / measC == 1
        nTrue++
      if dd(seqIdx, O_R3Y, O_R2Y) / measC - burstN == -1 and dd(seqIdx, O_R4Y, O_R3Y) / measC - burstN == 0 and dd(seqIdx, O_R5Y, O_R4Y) / measC == 1
        nCarry++
    debug("ACCY: TRUE (lag) pair in ", udec_(nTrue), " of 16, carry arm TRUE in ", udec_(nCarry), " of 16 (see dy rows for the rest)")


{ MEASURING ENGINE -- runs in its own cog; the ONLY code that touches the
  streamer. No debug() here (DEBUG_COGS excludes this cog anyway).
  PTRA = @mbox on entry.
}
DAT             org     0        ' ---- Measuring Engine ----
engine          mov     ptrb, ptra
                add     ptrb, #HDR * 4          ' records start at mbox[HDR]
                setluts #0                      ' LUT sharing OFF (reset state)
                setxfrq freq80_                 ' $8000_0000 = reset value; no SETQ anywhere
                wrpin   #0, #PIN                ' P3: reset config (smart pin off, logic input)

                ' write the LUT long at ALL 512 addresses, once, before any burst
                mov     ii_, #$1FF
.fill           wrlut   lutv_, ii_
                djnf    ii_, #.fill

                ' read three addresses back into the header (gated by cog 0)
                rdlut   t1_, laddr_
                rdlut   t2_, a000_
                rdlut   t3_, a1ff_
                mov     t0_, ptra
                add     t0_, #4
                wrlong  t1_, t0_
                add     t0_, #4
                wrlong  t2_, t0_
                add     t0_, #4
                wrlong  t3_, t0_

                drvl    #PIN                    ' DIR=1, OUT=0
                waitx   ##WAIT_PIN

                ' prime: a zero burst sets the held term to zero whatever it was,
                ' and leaves the LUT read path holding our long
                xinit   dz_, imz_
                waitx   ##WAIT_IDLE

                mov     level_, #0
.lvl            cmp     level_, #0              wz
        if_z    drvl    #PIN                    ' P3 LOW  -> predicted C = -g
        if_nz   drvh    #PIN                    ' P3 HIGH -> predicted C = +g
                waitx   ##WAIT_PIN
                mov     rep_, #REPS
.rep            mov     nn_, #N_A
                call    #do_seq
                mov     nn_, #N_B
                call    #do_seq
                djnz    rep_, #.rep
                add     level_, #1
                cmp     level_, #2              wz
        if_nz   jmp     #.lvl

                wrlong  #MBOX_DONE, ptra         ' done -- always the last write
                cogid   t1_
                cogstop t1_                     ' releases P3

'' One sequence for burst length nn_. Every GETXACC is issued with the streamer
'' idle (WAIT_IDLE clocks after the XINIT). "mov y, 0-0" receives accy.
do_seq          mov     dk_, dmode_
                or      dk_, nn_                ' D = $F007_0000 + N
                testp   #PIN                    wc
                wrc     pinb_

                getxacc b0x_                    ' B0
                mov     b0y_, 0-0

                xinit   dz_, imz_               ' START: zero burst
                waitx   ##WAIT_IDLE
                getxacc bx_                     ' B
                mov     by_, 0-0

                xinit   dk_, imk_               ' BURST: count N, imm[15]=1
                waitx   ##WAIT_IDLE
                getxacc r1x_                    ' R1
                mov     r1y_, 0-0
                waitx   ##WAIT_R1B
                getxacc r1bx_                   ' R1b, 1000 clocks later
                mov     r1by_, 0-0

                xinit   dz_, imz_               ' IDIOM: zero burst
                waitx   ##WAIT_IDLE
                getxacc r2x_                    ' R2
                mov     r2y_, 0-0

                xinit   dk_, imk_               ' CARRY ARM: K burst
                waitx   ##WAIT_IDLE
                getxacc r3x_                    ' R3
                mov     r3y_, 0-0

                xinit   dk_, imk_               ' second K burst right after
                waitx   ##WAIT_IDLE
                getxacc r4x_                    ' R4
                mov     r4y_, 0-0

                xinit   dz_, imz_               ' zero burst flushes
                waitx   ##WAIT_IDLE
                getxacc r5x_                    ' R5
                mov     r5y_, 0-0

                testp   #PIN                    wc
                wrc     pina_
                mov     rlevel_, level_
                mov     rn_, nn_
                setq    #RECL - 1               ' block-write the 20-long record
                wrlong  rlevel_, ptrb
                add     ptrb, #RECL * 4
                ret

freq80_         long    $8000_0000
lutv_           long    LUTV
laddr_          long    LUT_ADDR
a000_           long    0
a1ff_           long    $1FF
dmode_          long    MODE_G
dz_             long    MODE_G | ZCOUNT
imz_            long    IMM_Z
imk_            long    IMM_K

ii_             res     1
t0_             res     1
t1_             res     1
t2_             res     1
t3_             res     1
level_          res     1
rep_            res     1
nn_             res     1
dk_             res     1
' ---- the record: order MUST match O_LEVEL..O_R5Y ----
rlevel_         res     1
rn_             res     1
pinb_           res     1
pina_           res     1
b0x_            res     1
b0y_            res     1
bx_             res     1
by_             res     1
r1x_            res     1
r1y_            res     1
r1bx_           res     1
r1by_           res     1
r2x_            res     1
r2y_            res     1
r3x_            res     1
r3y_            res     1
r4x_            res     1
r4y_            res     1
r5x_            res     1
r5y_            res     1

